the kaiapoi west regeneration area of  approximately two point six hectares  comprises a rectangular block of land  bounded by raven key and hilton street  to the north and south and by rich  street and black street to the west and  east murphy park and a kaiapoi river lie  to the north of the area traveling in a  southwesterly direction from the  mandeville footbridge across the area  the first part of the area has been  identified as suitable for business use  which could include vehicle parking or  yard based activities such as a plant  nursery or a car sales yard the land in  the second part of the area which is  bisected by the Dudley drain we're  planting enhancement as proposed has  been identified as suitable for a sport  and recreation reserve users could be a  lawn based sports club or overflow  parking venir by Murphy park or a  playground area or a turf area for  informal ball play or the installation  of paths seating and planting we'd like  your comments on these regeneration area  proposals for full details of all the  options outlined in let's plan or to  comment on the plan visit the council  website at Waimakariri govt TN z or red  zone plan ends it will pick up a copy  from any council service center or  library
 

